Decoder logic is byte-for-byte equivalent to the upstream JavaScript
source. Modifications: ported to TypeScript (explicit types on
parameters, locals, return values), Biome-style formatting (2-space
indent, double quotes, trailing commas, semicolons), and `as number` /
`as Float32Array` casts to satisfy `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` without
using non-null assertions. No algorithmic changes.
